## Project Structure

```
/app
  /admin              ← Payload admin (auto-generated)
  /(site)
    layout.tsx        ← Root layout — mounts WeatherBackground once
    page.tsx          ← Single page, all sections rendered in order
/components
  /WeatherBackground  ← Canvas-based pixel art scene, weather + time driven
  /Nav
  /sections
    /Hero
    /About
    /Expertise
    /Career
    /Projects
    /Contact
/payload
  /collections        ← One file per Payload collection
/styles
  _variables.scss
  _reset.scss
  _typography.scss
  _main.scss          ← Entry point, imports partials
/lib
  /weather.ts         ← Open-Meteo fetch + geolocation utility
  /payload.ts         ← Payload query helpers
/__tests__            ← Unit and integration tests mirror /lib and /components structure
/e2e                  ← Playwright tests
```

---

## Testing

Testing is not optional. Every meaningful piece of logic ships with tests.

### Testing Stack

| Concern | Tool |
|---|---|
| Unit tests (utils, helpers, logic) | **Vitest** |
| Component tests (rendering, interaction) | **React Testing Library + Vitest** |
| E2E tests (user flows, full page) | **Playwright** |
| API / Payload routes | **Vitest + supertest** |

### Rules

- **Unit test everything in `/lib`** — weather normalisation, CMS helpers, date/time utilities
- **Component tests** cover: renders correctly, handles loading/error states, user interactions fire correct callbacks — not implementation details
- **Don't test the framework** — testing that `useState` updates is not a test
- Test behaviour, not structure — querying by role/label not by class or test ID unless unavoidable
- E2E covers critical paths: page loads, sections visible, weather component initialises, contact link works
- Aim for tests that would catch a real regression, not tests that inflate coverage numbers
- Co-locate component tests: `WeatherBackground.test.tsx` sits next to `WeatherBackground.tsx`

```
/components/WeatherBackground/
  WeatherBackground.tsx
  WeatherBackground.test.tsx
  WeatherBackground.module.scss
  index.ts
```

---

## WeatherBackground Component

The signature centrepiece of the site. Rules for working on it:

- Renders a **pixel art scene** (HTML5 Canvas or PixiJS — TBD) of a figure at a campfire in a forest clearing
- Weather state derived from **Open-Meteo** using browser Geolocation API on mount
- Time of day derived from **local system clock**
- Prop: `weatherState: 'clear' | 'cloudy' | 'rain' | 'storm' | 'snow'`
- Mounts **once** in root layout — never unmounts between section scrolls
- Fixed, full-viewport, `z-index: 0` — content panels sit above it
- Fetches weather once on mount, refreshes every 30 minutes — not on every render
- Graceful fallback: if geolocation denied or API fails, defaults to `clear` at current local time

---

## Git

- Conventional commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `refactor:`, `test:`, `docs:`
- No commits with broken tests
- Branch naming: `feature/`, `fix/`, `chore/`
- PRs (even solo) — keeps the history readable

---

## What to Always Ask Before Doing

- Adding a new dependency
- Adding anything to global context or a Payload collection
- Creating a new custom hook
- Reaching for a third-party solution when a small utility would do
- Adding a new top-level directory

---

## What to Never Do Without Being Asked

- Add comments explaining what code does (only why)
- Add loading spinners/skeletons unless the section specifically needs them
- Abstract prematurely — duplication is better than the wrong abstraction
- Generate placeholder/lorem ipsum content
- Add `console.log` statements to committed code